# Beef & Noodles — Freezer Meal (Dutch Oven or Ninja Foodi)

A slow-braised, tender beef and noodle dish designed for Sunday prep, freezer storage, and dump-and-cook weeknights.

## Ingredients
- 2 lbs stew beef  
- 1 large onion, sliced  
- 3 cloves garlic, minced  
- 4 cups beef broth (plus extra for cooking day)  
- 2 tbsp Worcestershire sauce  
- 1 tbsp soy sauce (optional)  
- 1 tsp salt  
- 1/2 tsp black pepper  
- 1 bag egg noodles (added on cooking day)

## Freezer Prep (Sunday)
1. Add stew beef, onion, garlic, broth, Worcestershire, soy sauce, salt, and pepper into a large freezer bag or freezer-safe container.  
2. Seal well and freeze flat.  
3. Label with:
   - “Beef & Noodles — cook from frozen”
   - “Add egg noodles at end”
   - “Dutch oven: 300°F for 3.5–4 hrs”
   - “Ninja Foodi: Pressure cook 45 min + 3 min for noodles”

## Cooking From Frozen — Dutch Oven
1. Place the frozen block into a Dutch oven.  
2. Add 1/2–1 cup extra broth.  
3. Cover and cook at 300°F for 3.5–4 hours  
   - OR 275°F for 5 hours for extra tenderness.  
4. When beef is tender, add egg noodles and 1–2 cups broth.  
5. Cover and cook 15–20 minutes, until noodles are soft.

## Cooking From Frozen — Ninja Foodi
1. Place frozen block into the pot.  
2. Pressure cook 45 minutes; allow natural release.  
3. Add egg noodles
